run 7 — why has the weekly warehouse maintenance never fired? Read both apps' WORKER_QUEUES.

Run #16 of Production logs (2026-09-20, 14d window) found `maintenance-run`
ABSENT across a window containing BOTH Sunday 03:00 slots (09-13 and 09-20).
That line — 'warehouse maintenance start', warehouseMaintenance.ts:169 — is
logged unconditionally at the top of runMaintenance, before any Delta work, so
its absence is not "nothing to maintain": the job is not executing.

Registration is already ruled out from the code: loadSchedules() calls
registerWeeklyMaintenance() immediately before registerDailyBrief(), in the
same function past the same early return, and `brief-run` demonstrably fires
in production. So the repeatable is registered and something downstream of
that is not running it.

The leading candidate is queue ownership. `warehouse-maintenance` is in
COMPUTE_QUEUES (queueRoles.ts), so startMaintenanceWorker() returns null in
any process whose WORKER_QUEUES excludes it. The API was pinned to the five
identity-requiring queues on 2026-09-01; if the jobs-worker's WORKER_QUEUES
does not include `warehouse-maintenance`, NO process consumes that queue and
the weekly job sits unpromoted forever — which would match exactly what run
#16 saw.

This probe is read-only. What settles it is two lines of its output:
  - backend WORKER_QUEUES
  - worker  WORKER_QUEUES
If neither contains `warehouse-maintenance` (and the worker's is not unset,
which means all), that is the bug and the fix is one env var.
